{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"toolshed_web_search","tool":"call_web_search","arguments":{"fast_mode":false,"web_search_instructions":"Find current authoritative Scalable Press API v2 documentation for creating DTG designs, quotes, and test/sandbox orders, including authentication syntax, request fields, whether test API keys can safely submit orders, and current product IDs for black fitted/unisex t-shirts. Provide concise results with source URLs."},"result":null,"error":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"toolshed_web_search","tool":"call_web_search","arguments":{"fast_mode":false,"web_search_instructions":"Find current authoritative Scalable Press API v2 documentation for creating DTG designs, quotes, and test/sandbox orders, including authentication syntax, request fields, whether test API keys can safely submit orders, and current product IDs for black fitted/unisex t-shirts. Provide concise results with source URLs."},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Research Report: Scalable Press API v2 Documentation for DTG Designs, Quotes, and Test/Sandbox Orders\n\n## Executive Summary\n\nScalable Press provides a comprehensive API v2 that enables users to create Direct-to-Garment (DTG) designs, obtain quotes, and place test or sandbox orders. The API utilizes HTTP Basic Authentication, requiring an API key. Test API keys can safely submit orders in test mode without actual fulfillment. Product IDs for black fitted/unisex t-shirts are available in the product catalog.\n\n## Key Findings\n\n- **Finding 1:** The Scalable Press API v2 allows for the creation of DTG designs by uploading artwork files with specified dimensions and placements.\n\n- **Finding 2:** Users can obtain exact quotes before placing orders through the Quote API, which provides detailed pricing information and indicates whether the provided data is sufficient for order placement.\n\n- **Finding 3:** Authentication is handled via HTTP Basic Authentication, where the API key is used as the password, and the username is left blank.\n\n- **Finding 4:** Test API keys enable users to submit orders in test mode, allowing for safe testing without actual fulfillment.\n\n- **Finding 5:** Product IDs for black fitted/unisex t-shirts can be found in the Scalable Press product catalog, accessible through the API.\n\n---\n\n## Detailed Source Analysis\n\n### Source 1: API Documentation\n\n- **URL:** https://scalablepress.com/docs/\n\n- **Domain:** scalablepress.com\n\n- **Publication Date:** Date not specified\n\n- **Source Type:** Official Documentation\n\n- **Credibility:** High (Official documentation from Scalable Press)\n\n**Summary:**\n\nThe Scalable Press API documentation provides detailed information on creating DTG designs, obtaining quotes, and placing orders. To create a design, users upload an artwork file along with dimensions and placement specifications, resulting in a design object that can be used for quotes, mockups, and orders. The Quote API offers exact quotes before order placement, indicating whether the provided information is sufficient for an actual order. Authentication requires HTTP Basic Authentication, using the API key as the password and leaving the username blank. Test API keys allow for order submission in test mode without actual fulfillment.\n\n**Key Data Points:**\n\n- Design creation involves uploading artwork with specified dimensions and placements.\n\n- The Quote API provides detailed pricing and order readiness status.\n\n- Authentication uses HTTP Basic Authentication with the API key as the password.\n\n- Test API keys enable safe testing without actual fulfillment.\n\n**Notable Quotes:**\n\n> \"Upload an artwork file, along with dimensions and placement specifications, to create a design object.\"\n\n> \"The Quote API lets you get an exact quote before placing an order.\"\n\n---\n\n### Source 2: Scalable Press Product Catalog\n\n- **URL:** https://scalablepress.com/catalog\n\n- **Domain:** scalablepress.com\n\n- **Publication Date:** Date not specified\n\n- **Source Type:** Product Catalog\n\n- **Credibility:** High (Official product catalog from Scalable Press)\n\n**Summary:**\n\nThe Scalable Press product catalog features over 4,000 products, including various styles of t-shirts. Users can search for specific products by name or SKU to find product IDs. This resource is essential for identifying the correct product IDs needed when creating designs and placing orders through the API.\n\n**Key Data Points:**\n\n- Over 4,000 products are available in the catalog.\n\n- Users can search by name or SKU to find product IDs.\n\n**Notable Quotes:**\n\n> \"Explore our product catalog featuring 4,000+ products.\"\n\n---\n\n### Source 3: Scalable Press API Overview\n\n- **URL:** https://scalablepress.com/api\n\n- **Domain:** scalablepress.com\n\n- **Publication Date:** Date not specified\n\n- **Source Type:** API Overview\n\n- **Credibility:** High (Official API overview from Scalable Press)\n\n**Summary:**\n\nThe Scalable Press API enables programmatic ordering of customized products, including t-shirts, mugs, phone cases, and posters. It supports various printing methods such as DTG, screen printing, and sublimation. The API is designed for developers to integrate product customization and fulfillment into their applications, offering features like design creation, quoting, and order tracking.\n\n**Key Data Points:**\n\n- Supports multiple product types and printing methods.\n\n- Designed for developer integration into applications.\n\n**Notable Quotes:**\n\n> \"Programmatically send t-shirts, mugs, phone cases, posters, and 4000 other products.\"\n\n---\n\n## Cross-Reference Analysis\n\n**Consensus Across Sources:**\n\n- All sources confirm that the Scalable Press API v2 supports the creation of DTG designs, obtaining quotes, and placing orders.\n\n- Authentication is consistently described as requiring HTTP Basic Authentication with the API key as the password.\n\n**Conflicting Information:**\n\n- No conflicting information was identified across the sources.\n\n**Information Gaps:**\n\n- Specific product IDs for black fitted/unisex t-shirts are not directly provided in the available sources.\n\n- Detailed information on the limitations or restrictions of test API keys is not extensively covered.\n\n---\n\n## Research Metadata\n\n- **Search Completed:** 2026-08-22T22:43:53Z\n\n- **Sources Analyzed:** 3 sources\n\n- **Total Content Reviewed:** Approximately 1,200 words� "}],"_meta":{"openai/widgetSessionId":"60817e9e-5a14-4422-bd10-b2a786acf883"},"structured_content":null},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
